## Tower Crane In Use

This project opts into reusable Claude Code tooling from the Tower Crane hub. These are
referenced (float-on-HEAD), not copied — an update ratified in the hub reaches this project the
next time it runs. This machine's copy of the hub lives wherever `.claude/hub_pointer.md` (this
project's own gitignored, per-host pointer file) currently records — see that file's
`shared_root:` value for the real path, or the hub's own `MENU.md` there for the full catalog. Do
not edit the shared files; to report a bug or request an improvement, follow the filing protocol
imported below. Tower Crane keeps everything it manages in this file directive-only, with
narrative in `README.md` and a decisions/activity log in `project_progress.md` if this project
uses them — its own convention for its own content, not a requirement for anything else in this
file.

Whether this file is actually live on **this** machine right now is decided by one thing: does
`.claude/hub_pointer.md` (gitignored, per-host, never itself tracked — regenerated by `"connect
project"`/`relocate.py`) exist? If it does, read it for the real hub path and this machine's host
identity, and everything below applies. If it doesn't, Tower Crane is not connected on this
machine, full stop — none of the host-specific behavior below applies, and there is no need (and
no reliable way) to determine which machine this is instead. Don't guess.

If it doesn't exist, the following may still be present on disk (left behind, or live for a
*different* connected host sharing this same repo) but are inert here — ignore them, don't try to
use or explain them: everything under `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/hooks/_hub_dispatch.py`, any
`.claude/settings.json` hook entry invoking `_hub_dispatch.py` plus its `Read(...)` permission
line, and the `@import`/`@.claude/hub_pointer.md` line at the top of this file.

